# .prettierignore
# Build output and generated files. Formatting these is pointless at best and
# destructive at worst — www/browser is the compiled app, and prettier-plugin-
# organize-imports would rewrite imports inside bundled output.

www/
dist/
android/
ios/
.angular/
node_modules/
functions/lib/
functions/node_modules/

# package-lock.json is generated and must not be reformatted; npm owns it.
package-lock.json
functions/package-lock.json

# Firestore rules: hand-written with deliberate alignment in the comment blocks.
# Prettier has no parser for the rules language and would either fail or mangle it.
firestore.rules

# The audit documents in Docs/ are historical records. Reformatting them would
# make them differ from the state they describe, for no benefit.
Docs/

# Gap-analysis artefacts checked in as input to past reviews.
repomix-output.xml

# Prettier has no parser for .editorconfig and fails the whole run on it with
# "Invalid or unexpected token". It is not a format prettier can express anyway.
.editorconfig

# The linter and formatter configs are CommonJS with block comments, because the
# reasoning behind each setting is worth more than the setting. Prettier's own
# parser for .js does not accept a comment-free-required module the way it
# expects for a config file, so these are excluded and formatted by hand. There
# are two files; hand-formatting them is not a burden.
.eslintrc.js
.prettierrc.js
.lintstagedrc.js

# Dotfiles with no file extension. Prettier has no parser for them and guesses
# the babel parser, which fails on JSON and plain text alike. They are all
# config: .firebaserc, .nvmrc, .npmrc, .firebaserc.alias.*
.*